Windows build: a 64-bit-clean handle cast in DxgiFns.cpp

The Windows virgl changes (0003) pass the winsys handle, a pointer-sized value, to a 32-bit
D3DKMT_HANDLE; clang rejects the direct cast in C++ on 64-bit. Cast through uintptr_t.

diff -ru a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/DxgiFns.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/DxgiFns.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/DxgiFns.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/DxgiFns.cpp
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@
       return S_OK;
    };
 
-   device->device.base.setDisplayMode(&device->device.base, (D3DKMT_HANDLE)handle.handle);
+   device->device.base.setDisplayMode(&device->device.base, (D3DKMT_HANDLE)(uintptr_t)handle.handle);
 
    return S_OK;
 }
